# Thriden host checkout -- ignore the deploy tooling's own working files.
#
# Published to the PUBLIC Digital-Heresy/Thriden mirror AS `.gitignore` by
# .github/workflows/sync-thriden-deploy.yml (an explicit rename, exactly like
# README.md / LICENSE). It is deliberately NOT listed in
# .github/thriden-deploy-manifest.txt: that allowlist copies paths verbatim and
# has no rename support, and a second `.gitignore` cannot live at this repo root.
#
# WHY a purpose-built file rather than shipping MindHive's own .gitignore:
# ours names venv/, engram/target/, node_modules/, dist/beta-participants/ and
# the rest of the dev tree, which discloses repo structure the "lean public"
# posture deliberately withholds (docs/beta-onboarding-design.md, the same
# reason docs/ and the operator runbooks do not ship).
#
# WHAT it is for: thriden-doctor.sh check 9 reports stray untracked files so a
# genuine stray stays visible (the '&1' incident -- a stray shell-redirect
# file). Every path below is created by our OWN tooling on a correctly
# functioning host, so without these rules check 9 WARNs forever and trains the
# operator to read a non-green doctor as normal -- which is precisely the state
# a real stray hides in. Measured on Cairn: 9 PASS / 1 WARN, nine listed files,
# all ours.
#
# ⚠ NO RULE HERE MAY MATCH A PATH IN .github/thriden-deploy-manifest.txt.
# The mirror publish step runs `git add -A` with this file already staged, so a
# rule matching a NEWLY added manifest path would silently drop that file from
# the mirror -- and the manifest's fail-closed check cannot catch it, because it
# verifies the path exists in MindHive, not that it landed upstream. Already-
# shipped paths are safe (they are in the mirror's index, where gitignore does
# not apply), which is what makes this fail only for a future addition, and only
# once. The workflow's "Assert every staged file landed in the mirror index"
# step checks the end state directly; keep it if you edit this list.

# Host-local config the operator creates by following the onboarding guide.
.env
.env.*
.sops.yaml
.thriden-host-short

# The operator's own SOPS-encrypted secrets tree. Theirs, never ours, and it
# must never be pushed anywhere. (On a DH host that clones MindHive instead of
# the mirror these files are TRACKED, so this rule is inert there and check 9
# keeps its own secrets/ exclusion for the sops re-encryption noise -- see the
# note in bin/thriden-doctor.sh check 9.)
secrets/

# Isolated docker config dir, created by bin/thriden-compose-pull.sh so the GHCR
# login never touches the operator's real ~/.docker/config.json.
.docker/

# Pre-flight /admin/export target (bin/thriden-deploy-payload.sh).
backups/

# Per-Scion compose drop-in, written by bin/thriden-scion-up.sh.
# HYPHEN, not dot: this must not match the shipped compose.prod.yml, and it does
# not match docker-compose.yml either (a no-slash pattern must match the whole
# basename, which here has to start with `compose-`).
compose-*.yml

# Deploy-payload working files (bin/thriden-deploy-payload.sh). The second glob
# is redundant against manifest-*.json and is spelled out anyway, because the
# .result.json siblings are the ones that accumulate.
payloads/
manifest-*.json
manifest-*.result.json
